n seat after Republican Ashley Hinson left it to run for Senate, and it has become one of the cycle's most competitive House races. The district carries a Republican lean of about four points, but the 2026 national environment has favored Democrats, and independent analysts are nearly unanimous in calling the race a tossup. A July poll sponsored by Democratic groups showed Lindsay James narrowly ahead of Joe Mitchell, though that survey is the only recent public data and is already months old.\n\nBoth candidates have raised more than $1.6 million, with Mitchell holding a modest cash edge while outside groups have directed most of their attacks at him. Prediction markets give the Democrat a slight edge, and the first debate centered on affordability, Iran and immigration without producing a clear pivot. The forecast expects a margin of about a point and a half for James, with wide uncertainty; this remains a genuine coin flip heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5595, "margin": 0.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5585, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6246, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.619, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5799, "margin": 1.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.557, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6133, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6185, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6098, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5891, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6068, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.615, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6272, "margin": 1.5}]}